# Refresh dirty open PRs (`/iflow-pr-sync`)

`/iflow-pr-sync` brings **open PR heads** up to date with the default branch after
another merge left them `DIRTY` / “needs update” — almost always because both
sides edited `{{ history_file }}`.

It is **off-path** (never auto-run by `/iflow`). Prefer it over clicking GitHub’s
Update branch when the conflict is changelog bookkeeping.

{% include "skills/_model_directive.md.j2" %}

{% include "skills/_resolve_project_root.md.j2" %}

## Input

- Nothing → every open PR GitHub marks as needing update.
- PR numbers → only those (e.g. `/iflow-pr-sync 259`).
- `dry-run` → list only.
- `nopush` → sync without pushing.
- `all` → every open PR.

## What the assistant does

1. Prefers standing on the default branch; fetches.
2. Lists candidates via `issue-flow agent pr-sync --dry-run --json`.
3. One consolidated confirm (rebase/merge onto default + `--force-with-lease`).
4. Runs `issue-flow agent pr-sync …` (reuses `sync-branch` keep-both).
5. Reports per-PR results; does not merge.

## Constraints

- Never bare `--force`, never `--admin`, never skip checks.
- Fail-fast on non-auto-resolvable conflicts.
- Design: `{{ issueflows_dir }}/{{ designs_folder }}/pr-queue-sync.md`.
